'' WCHR had no lowering at all, so 'w = wchr( n )' declined and so did every term built
'' out of one. It is the wide twin of CHR and variadic like it -- fb_WstrChr( count,
'' code... ), measured -- and its TYPE is 'WSTRING * (argc + 1)', measured with
'' '#print typeof': the terminator counts.
''
'' A WIDE VALUE APPENDED TO A USTRING IS A CONVERSION, not a concatenation: a wstring
'' is a bare uint16* and a ustring a DESCRIPTOR, and no entry point takes one and
'' appends to the other. Measured:
''
''     vr$2 = fb_WstrChr( 1, QUOTE );
''     vr$3 = fb_WstrToUStr( vr$2 );
''     fb_UStrConcatAssign( &CUR$0, -1, vr$3, -1, 0 );
''
'' -- which is how fb/string.bi appends 'wchr( QUOTE )' to the ustring it is building,
'' on the line its own comment insists must be WCHR and never CHR.
''
'' ONE DIVERGENCE, deliberate: fbc FOLDS 'wchr( 65 )' over a literal to a wide literal
'' and emits no call. tiko-lang always calls. Same value, different code.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/wchr.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrChr
'' GOLDEN: expected/wchr.out
